#====================================================================
# DRAFT-expat-cmake-soname-1912 - Disable CMake versioned shared-library symlinks on OHOS paths
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-expat-cmake-soname-1912
trigger_tool:           cmake|conan|ld.lld|readelf
phase:                  build|package|testing
error_signature:        failed to create symbolic link .*\.so\.[0-9]+|cmake_symlink_library: System Error: Permission denied|DT_NEEDED.*\.conan2

severity:               2
category:               cmake|shared-library|soname|ohos-filesystem
match_keywords:         CMake, SONAME, symlink, cmake_symlink_library, CMAKE_PLATFORM_NO_VERSIONED_SONAME, CMAKE_SHARED_LIBRARY_SONAME_C_FLAG, DT_NEEDED, HMDFS, expat
title:                  Disable CMake versioned shared-library symlinks on OHOS paths

root_cause:             CMake's Unix shared-library rules can create versioned .so names and symlinks. OHOS/HMDFS-backed build paths can reject symlink creation even when the compiled shared object is valid. Disabling SONAME entirely avoids symlink creation but can make downstream DT_NEEDED entries record an absolute Conan cache path.
affected_scope:         CMake packages that produce versioned shared libraries on HarmonyOS PC or OHOS/HMDFS paths, especially libraries consumed by downstream shared objects.
verification_cmd:       Run clean conan create on HarmonyOS PC CI or target runner; require build/install to pass, llvm-readelf -d to show Library soname: [libexpat.so], and Conan test_package to dlopen and call real APIs.

rec_priority:           1
rec_approach:           no-versioned-soname-keep-soname-flag
rec_description:        Set CMAKE_PLATFORM_NO_VERSIONED_SONAME=ON while keeping CMAKE_SHARED_LIBRARY_SONAME_C_FLAG=-Wl,-soname, so CMake emits an unversioned real .so with a relocatable ELF SONAME and does not create versioned symlinks.
rec_command:            -DCMAKE_PLATFORM_NO_VERSIONED_SONAME=ON -DCMAKE_SHARED_LIBRARY_SONAME_C_FLAG=-Wl,-soname,
rec_auto_fix:           false
rec_impl:               conan-recipe

fallback_priority:      2
fallback_approach:      package-unversioned-shared-library-with-explicit-runtime-validation
fallback_description:   If the project cannot use CMAKE_PLATFORM_NO_VERSIONED_SONAME, package an unversioned shared object through the upstream-supported install path and explicitly verify DT_NEEDED/SONAME and runtime loading on target.
fallback_command:       llvm-readelf -d libfoo.so
fallback_auto_fix:      false
fallback_impl:          package-validation

forbid_1_pattern:       CMAKE_SKIP_RPATH|CMAKE_NO_SONAME|NO_SONAME
forbid_1_reason:        Removing SONAME emission can make downstream DT_NEEDED entries capture a non-relocatable package-cache path.
forbid_1_consequence:   Consumers can work only while the exact Conan cache path exists and fail after cache cleanup, revision changes, or machine changes.

forbid_2_pattern:       rm .*lib.*\.so\.[0-9]+|unlink .*\.so\.[0-9]+
forbid_2_reason:        Deleting symlinks in package() cannot fix a build that already fails during CMake's build-time symlink creation.
forbid_2_consequence:   The recipe remains flaky or fails before package cleanup runs.

principles:             P010, P012
